---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Industries
permalink: /industries/
description: Reference system blueprints by sector — logistics, clinics, law, security, construction, real estate, education, accounting, automotive, and recruitment.
---

<section class="pagehead">
  <div class="hero__grid-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="pagehead__scene" data-scene data-scene-density="low" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
    <span class="label label--signal">Blueprint layer</span>
    <h1 class="h1" style="margin-top:1rem">Industries</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
      Every sector leaks work in its own places. These are the systems I build
      for each one &mdash; what goes on the public site, what runs behind it,
      and what stops being anyone&rsquo;s job to remember.
    </p>

    <div class="pagehead__meta">
      <span class="label label--faint">{{ industries.length }} sectors</span>
      <span class="label label--faint">Reference architectures</span>
      <span class="label label--faint">Built to order</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="label">Sector index</span>
      <span class="eyebrow__rule"></span>
      <span class="label label--plain label--faint">Select a blueprint</span>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      {% for industry in industries %}
        <a class="card industry-card" href="/industries/{{ industry.slug }}/"
           data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index0 * 55 }}">
          <div class="card__body">
            <span class="label label--signal">{{ industry.sector }}</span>
            <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top:1rem">{{ industry.name }}</h2>
            <p class="industry-card__tagline">{{ industry.tagline }}</p>
            <p class="body body--sm" style="margin-top:.9rem">{{ industry.summary }}</p>

            <ul class="industry-card__leaks">
              {% for leak in industry.leaks | slice_first(3) %}
                <li>{{ leak.title }}</li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card__foot">
            <span class="label label--faint">{{ loop.index0 | pad }}</span>
            <span class="label label--plain label--faint">
              {{ industry.build.public.length + industry.build.portal.length }} modules
              <span class="btn__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--dark section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__lead">
        <h2 class="h2">Your sector is not on the list?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
          The pattern holds regardless of trade: find where work waits on a
          person to remember it, then build the thing that remembers instead.
          Run the diagnostic on your current site, or describe the operation.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem">
          <button type="button" class="btn" data-open-diagnostic>
            Run diagnostic <span class="btn__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
          </button>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/start/">
            Describe the operation <span class="btn__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
